@@ -0,0 +1,9 @@
+# Registered sign context observations
+
+Twenty-four diagnostic cases cross number versus length-or-number registration, direct versus unregistered-provider expression, positive/zero/negative em operands, and self-font versus fixed-font contexts. No expected CSS values or conformance assertions are embedded. The `+ 10` consumer offset avoids negative font-size grammar confounding the negative operand. Each case has two complete relevant snapshots, with parent font 19→29 and, for noncyclic controls, target font 20→30. All cases record raw provider text, registered value, target font/line-height/width, specified declarations, parent declarations/font, registration errors, and fixed query order.
+
+The captured source path `CalcNode::Sign` -> `CalcNodeLeaf::sign_from` can fold a relative-unit leaf using unitless_value before the proposed collector runs. These cases investigate whether that optimization changes existing contextual cycle behavior. The [Properties and Values API relative-unit cycle rule](https://drafts.css-houdini.org/css-properties-values-api-1/#dependency-cycles) is expressly scoped to descriptors containing a length or length-percentage component; therefore both syntax groups are retained and neither receives an invented oracle. A's v2 selected-token policy is intended to preserve selected lexical units independently of AST simplification. No browser execution or no-regression claim is made here.
+
+The page sets `window.observations`, matching the existing observation runners' data handoff. A root-owned controlled runner must bind source/binary/epoch/profile and capture original/candidate snapshots. It must compare observations rather than declare these disputed values conformance successes. Do not add this page to the A104 or B16 normative fixture without a separate scoped decision.
+
+`report.html` loads `report.js` directly, without an iframe. It posts `{observation: {userAgent, queryOrder, rows}}` to the sibling `result` endpoint, or `{error}` on setup failure. `observation-only.html` is the same measurement body without the reporting transport. There are 24 exact case IDs in CASES.json and 48 snapshots. The runner must require all IDs and both snapshot records, retain registration errors, and compare CSS observations exactly without expected-value gates.
