+Sixteen observation-only cases: eight registered-length admission/defaulting modes crossed with fixed versus self-dependent font-size, each under Zoom 1 then 2. No expected CSS or geometry values. Initial value10px; parent registered value20px; selected literal5px. The ready-unused-em and rejected em cases target loss of accidental prioritary readiness; direct literal/invalid and initial/inherit/unset cases calibrate existing defaulting behavior. All registration errors and both snapshots are retained.
+
+report.html/report.js post {observation:{userAgent,queryOrder,rows}} or {error} to sibling result. validate.py checks exact16case identities and32snapshot shapes and compares all rows without a normative gate. It checks computed registered serialization, raw provider, font-size, line-height, width, zoom, and physical bounding-box width/height. The latter distinguish computed CSS serialization from physical scaling. Root must bind actual native/binary/epoch state; this package launches nothing.
+
+Source concern is conditional: captured NoCalcLength::to_computed_value_for_math scales absolute pixels by builder.effective_zoom. Captured apply_custom_and_prioritary_properties processes graph before remaining prioritary properties. Removing a font edge may alter readiness, but neither an observed difference nor a normative oracle is assumed. The variable serialization/resolved-value conversion chain still needs precise interpretation. Preserve full raw output and compare paired phases before attributing a regression.
+
+Node syntax and Python controls pass ad831e/0:256actual-field changes detected,16registration changes detected,64malformed captures rejected. No browser execution.
