+# Pending overlay compatibility
+
+The C++ overlay is unchanged: it appends two tests to the preserved fixture, retaining the original 20 tests and 22 resolver table rows. The candidate inventory is 22 tests and 34 source resolver calls. No runtime count is inferred from installation.
+
+Selected-token A preserves the pending prototype's existing broad numeric scheduling. The nine admission rows still exercise invalid selected values, unused fallbacks, pending-provider masking and CSS-wide values. Three math calls retain a real em/px endpoint across completion and font mutation; these are prototype capability checks, not acceptance of B scheduling into the standalone HEAD patch.
+
+The old validator's superseded custom/cascade/value pins are replaced in pending-validation-v2, bound to selected-token live proposal v3 with its CSS-wide lifetime repair. Its roster and assessment remain identical; fixed HEAD, original collector sources and all twenty required source pins are checked. Version 4 authenticates that package and requires every validator source hash to equal the planned post-overlay native pin or an unchanged current-epoch pin. The test overlay's exact roster must match the validator. The source epoch remains uncompiled until a subsequent build.
+
+This static compatibility does not establish compilation or native pass status. The bridge still cannot observe INHERITS_RESET_STYLE directly. Root owns all build and GTest execution; standalone A browser acceptance is separate.
