+# Selected-token admission source transition v4
+
+Prepared tool; no transition has run during its preparation. Freeze HEAD at `e2839ec561c1e19de963bd0d56f46f4c067685d0`. Version 4 binds the two-file selected-token A proposals and WPT capsule v4. It never installs the six-file semantic collector, whose original bytes and inodes are explicitly guarded throughout the operation.
+
+```text
+python3 -I -S -B artifacts/css-registered-number-source-transition-v4/transition.py TOOL_MANIFEST_SHA head-candidate CURRENT_EPOCH_SHA /Users/bgrins/code/firefox/artifacts/css-registered-number-wpt-runtime-original-3 ORIGINAL_RESULT_SHA head-candidate-1
+python3 -I -S -B artifacts/css-registered-number-source-transition-v4/transition.py TOOL_MANIFEST_SHA prototype-live CURRENT_EPOCH_SHA /Users/bgrins/code/firefox/artifacts/css-registered-number-wpt-runtime-candidate-2 CANDIDATE_RESULT_SHA prototype-live-1
+python3 -I -S -B artifacts/css-registered-number-source-transition-v4/transition.py TOOL_MANIFEST_SHA pending-tests RESTORED_EPOCH_SHA /Users/bgrins/code/firefox/artifacts/css-registered-number-native-runtime-v1/prototype-live-1 RESTORATION_RESULT_SHA pending-tests-1
+```
+
+Use independently recorded digests, the actual evidence directory, and absent output labels. The first mode requires compiled committed-HEAD original sources and a complete preserved original WPT observation. It changes exactly custom_properties.rs and properties/cascade.rs. The second requires compiled committed-HEAD candidate sources and complete preserved candidate WPT execution, restores all 50 parked prototype bodies, and overlays the exact two-file live A candidate. A completed preserved comparison with failing assertions can authorize restoration; it cannot confer acceptance. Both modes leave compilation and acceptance false and retain exactly 50 owned native files.
+
+The six collector source files are not acquired, changed, or added to pin maps. Two already appear in the saved epoch; four wrappers did not. For all six, v4 checks the fixed original hash, regular-file inode and HEAD blob in preflight, then checks bytes/inode immediately before native writes, after source changes, after metadata publication, and during rollback verification. The WPT capsule independently guards the same original bodies. Arbitrary other epoch pins and nested/index state remain guarded by the existing full preservation checker.
+
+All 140 recovery snapshot entries remain checked. For exactly CURRENT-COMMITS.json and PLAN-OF-RECORD.md, the authorized chain is v8 pin -> v14 before/preimage and after/selection -> v15 before/preimage and after/selection. Both signed checkpoint receipts/final checks, ten committed provenance blobs, and the explicit v15 prior-update pointer are bound. The final live/HEAD body and every matching epoch pin must equal the final after hash. No ledger is written by this tool. The other 138 checks use their parked or unchanged live bodies exactly as before; originally-clean value.rs now receives its ordinary original-body check because it is no longer a candidate file.
+
+`pending-tests` is enabled only with the sealed pending-validation-v2 package. Before installing the one-file overlay, the controller matches its frozen HEAD, six unchanged source guards, exact overlay roster, twenty source pins against the planned after-state, and the 22-test/34-source-call inventory. It requires the exact successful uncompiled prototype-live receipt and current epoch. Install the overlay before rebuilding the restored prototype; then run the independently guarded validator after that build. This mode still leaves compiled=false and accepted=false and records the bound validator manifest in its receipt. No native test is counted as executed by installation.
+
+Every enabled mode authenticates source packages/helper references, the external epoch SHA and exact source role, verifies full preservation before/after, preserves root/nested HEAD, index entries, cached diff and flags, and writes only owned regular-file inodes. Initial ROLE/OWNED bytes are bound to the authorization snapshot and rechecked before writes. Runtime metadata is published after source verification. The source write journal and preimages support owned rollback on exceptions/SIGTERM/SIGINT; rollback must restore the exact preservation snapshot and flags. Foreign inode/hash drift blocks destructive recovery and reports manual handling. SIGKILL/storage failure can leave a partial transition: inspect its journal and ownership; never bypass stale locks or digest gates.
+
+The lock coordinates this tool only. The parent must keep builds, browsers, signing and other publishers quiescent during execution. Recorded build/WPT process-group absence is checked. The full transition has not been executed in scratch or against the checkout; validation covers pure plan/receipt helpers and owned file writes, not a synthetic claim of native execution.
+
+Checks: 20 rejection controls for source/phase/ownership and disabled-mode rejection, 26 successor-chain controls, and 28 pending-validator planning controls; successful same-inode write/rollback and exact 50-file plans; all scratch removed. No live source, epoch, Git/index, binary, browser or build query/mutation was performed during preparation. Existing sealed v1/v2/v3 controllers and native proposals remain immutable.
+
+Capsule v4 can compare a fresh candidate against the strictly adopted byte-identical original-2 experiment. Adoption retains original capsule-v3 receipts unchanged and is explicit inside the new candidate receipt. The controller's head-candidate mode does not reinterpret those historical receipts: it requires a fresh original run from the matching active capsule. The current run has already installed the candidate, so prototype-live consumes the normal capsule-v4 candidate receipt; its additional original_adoption field does not relax source, epoch or lifecycle checks.
